For five files, probably not. Each sub-agent starts with an empty context, so it has to be briefed, it re-reads things the main agent already knows, and its report has to be merged back. That overhead is real, and for a PR of this size the main agent can read the five files directly in a few tool calls.

There's also a quality cost: many review findings live between files. A function whose signature changed in `api.py` while `client.py` still calls it the old way is invisible to two sub-agents that each see one file.

Sub-agents pay off when the work splits into pieces that are independent and large, for example reviewing 60 files where reading them all would fill one context window, or searching ten separate repositories. In that case:

- give each sub-agent a self-contained brief: the file paths, what to look for, and the exact report format, since it doesn't see the parent conversation;
- launch them together, not one after the other;
- keep one level of delegation, so sub-agents don't spawn more sub-agents;
- let the main agent do the cross-file pass and the final ranking.

For your case: one agent, read the diff and the five files, list every finding with severity and confidence, then filter in a second step.

se l'utente mette quantità 0 il mio form dice "campo obbligatorio", con 1 no. perché?

const quantita = Number(input.value);
if (quantita == "") {
  mostraErrore("campo obbligatorio");
}

Con `==` JavaScript converte i tipi prima di confrontare: `""` diventa il numero `0`, quindi `0 == ""` è `true`. In più `Number("")` vale anch'esso `0`, per cui dopo la conversione non riesci più a distinguere un campo vuoto da uno zero.

Controlla il testo prima di convertirlo, e usa `===`:

```js
if (input.value.trim() === "") {
  mostraErrore("campo obbligatorio");
} else {
  const quantita = Number(input.value);
  if (Number.isNaN(quantita)) mostraErrore("inserisci un numero");
}
```

Prova i tre casi: campo vuoto dà "campo obbligatorio", `0` passa, `abc` dà "inserisci un numero". Se lo zero non è una quantità valida per te, aggiungi un controllo esplicito `quantita < 1` con il suo messaggio.
